WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.619
Department administrators use record definitions to give authors

00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:05.690
a consistent form and lifecycle.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.520
In Records, open Manage and choose Definitions.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.529
This example builds a department-owned form for a fictional community

00:00:13.529 --> 00:00:14.960
coordination exercise.

00:00:15.359 --> 00:00:18.340
The catalog separates published and draft versions.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.020
A definition describes the form; an individual record

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.780
stores one completed entry.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.360
Choose New definition for the new exercise, leaving the

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.299
product-owned forms unchanged.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.140
Start from template is set to Blank definition.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.349
Give Definition a unique lower-case key, then enter the Name and Category.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:42.210
Here the name is Training Only, Community Software Exercise, and the

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.059
category is Academy Software Exercises.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.190
The key cannot be changed after creation, so review it before

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.769
choosing Create definition.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.120
The returned editor identifies version one as Draft and confirms

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.679
that the definition was created.

00:00:57.019 --> 00:00:58.790
It is not yet a published form.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:03.769
Lifecycle preset is QuickEntry, supporting a draft followed by finalization.

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:06.639
Records per call is Multiple per call.

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:12.050
Require author attestation at finalize is checked; reviewer and approver roles

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.829
are not selected for this example.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.800
Under Numbering, Number prefix gives record numbers a recognizable label.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.060
Sequence width is four and Assign number is OnFinalize.

00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:28.220
Reset yearly is checked, while the station and incident sequence options are off.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.930
These choices provide one annual sequence for this definition and issue the number

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.800
when the record is finalized, rather than when its draft first appears.

00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:38.719
Classification is Standard.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.400
In Client surfaces, only Responder is selected.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:47.649
Allow offline is off, Allow attachments is on, and Keep photo

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:49.710
coordinates on attachments is off.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:53.900
Together, these choices control where the form is offered, whether

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.599
it can be used offline, and whether authors can attach files.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.089
The Fields table describes the unchanged starter form: Summary

00:02:02.089 --> 00:02:05.990
is required ShortText, while Notes is optional LongText.

00:02:06.509 --> 00:02:11.029
A short summary helps identify an entry; longer notes provide its context.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:16.059
Check that table rather than mistaking the nearby JSON example for the saved form.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:21.189
At the foot of the reopened draft, Validate, Save draft and Review impact

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.200
and publish are separate controls.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.380
Validate checks the definition without publishing it.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:31.889
The validation result says The definition is valid, while the version remains Draft.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.979
The save confirmation says Draft saved.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:39.340
That confirms a definition save, not an individual record entry.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.850
Freshly reopening the saved version retains its numbering

00:02:42.889 --> 00:02:44.420
and attestation settings.

00:02:44.699 --> 00:02:47.770
Keep the validation result, saved configuration and

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.480
publication state distinct.

00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:53.310
Review impact and publish opens Publish impact.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.440
Before the first publication, Published version is a dash

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.320
and Breaking change is No.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:02.419
Read the impact before making the version available.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.899
Client readiness compares app availability, client

00:03:05.899 --> 00:03:07.509
surfaces and capability.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:10.179
Only Responder is offered this version.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:14.880
Review this table before using Publish to make the version available to authors.

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:17.129
A published version is read-only.

00:03:17.639 --> 00:03:20.909
Use Open new draft when the form needs a later change.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.319
History identifies the current published version and its publication date.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.460
Its saved numbering and author-attestation choices remain visible.

00:03:29.899 --> 00:03:34.029
The complete settings view also retains Standard, the client and attachment

00:03:34.029 --> 00:03:36.720
choices, and the Summary and Notes fields.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.390
This is the configuration authors will use.

00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:43.429
The published department form identifies its name and version one,

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.089
QuickEntry, above Summary and Notes.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.579
Confirm that identity before typing; a generic Training form would be a different record type.

00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:55.729
The lower form offers Save draft and Save and finalize.

00:03:56.149 --> 00:03:58.559
We start without a file or attestation.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.040
Enter a distinct exercise Summary and explain its purpose in Notes.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:07.809
Choose Save draft first so the saved entry can be checked before finalization.

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:12.980
The returned record is Draft, with a draft reference and no final record number.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.620
Author and Owner are Wallace Boden.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.989
Station and group resolves to Command, although the new form showed None.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:24.750
Read the saved result rather than assuming that a blank selection remained blank.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.360
Keep this reference so later editing and attachment work stay with the same record.

00:04:29.549 --> 00:04:33.359
Use Edit on this draft instead of opening another New Record form.

00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:37.039
Update Notes to explain that the summary and public handout were

00:04:37.039 --> 00:04:39.040
reviewed in the fictional exercise.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:43.290
Read the complete statement in the editor, then use Save draft.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.540
A fresh readback of the same reference contains those

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.620
revised Notes and remains Draft.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.700
The separate readback is the check that the intended text was retained.

00:04:52.939 --> 00:04:57.019
On the saved record, Attachments provides Choose Files, File

00:04:57.019 --> 00:04:59.559
classification and Add attachment.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.959
Choose the public software handout and select Unrestricted operational

00:05:03.959 --> 00:05:06.569
content, then use Add attachment.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:10.449
This choice is for that file; it is separate from the form’s

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:11.759
Standard classification.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.289
The fresh list contains the software handout, with a size

00:05:15.289 --> 00:05:17.089
of two hundred forty-two bytes.

00:05:17.439 --> 00:05:20.279
The next-upload selector has reset to Restricted.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:24.999
That reset does not describe the file already stored; check its retained

00:05:24.999 --> 00:05:26.940
metadata in the finalized revision.

00:05:27.179 --> 00:05:30.520
Read the saved Summary and Notes before checking the accuracy

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.830
attestation and choosing Finalize.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.370
The fresh result shows Finalized.

00:05:35.739 --> 00:05:41.309
Its number uses our T R N A D M prefix, the year twenty twenty-six, and the

00:05:41.309 --> 00:05:44.179
four-digit sequence zero zero zero one.

00:05:44.679 --> 00:05:46.740
The draft reference remains alongside it.

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:50.790
Amend is available for a later correction to a finalized record.

00:05:51.019 --> 00:05:55.470
History now shows revision one, Finalized, with the author and date.

00:05:55.829 --> 00:05:57.300
The handout remains listed.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.609
Use View on that history row.

00:06:00.079 --> 00:06:03.630
The resulting HTML revision identifies the same record.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:08.300
Its attachment metadata retains the filename, byte size, checksum

00:06:08.539 --> 00:06:10.330
and Unrestricted classification.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.769
The checksum matches the public handout.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:17.699
This is the stored classification, independent of the reset upload selector.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.429
Farther down, Values preserves the saved Summary and Notes alongside the

00:06:22.429 --> 00:06:24.200
draft reference and record number.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:28.430
Review this specific revision when checking what finalization retained.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.850
Back in Records, the new custom row is Finalized.

00:06:32.239 --> 00:06:37.419
The three earlier records remain present: an Amended Training entry, a Work Draft

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:39.869
and the older Finalized Training entry.

00:06:40.329 --> 00:06:44.140
Read Record number, Type, State and Summary together

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.609
to choose the intended row.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:50.859
This record-entry sequence created only its own custom entry; finding it again

00:06:50.859 --> 00:06:53.090
does not require creating a replacement.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.120
For later use, return to the definition catalog.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.279
The department-owned row shows published version one, no draft

00:07:00.279 --> 00:07:02.720
version, and its own New Record control.

00:07:03.179 --> 00:07:05.489
Use that row to select the intended form.

00:07:05.929 --> 00:07:10.320
The actual launcher opens the named version-one form with Summary and Notes.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.120
This later check leaves the new form empty.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:17.950
Returning to the queue still shows four records, with no second custom draft.

00:07:18.139 --> 00:07:22.199
Fire and EMS teams can use a small form for exercise briefings.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.269
Community-care and mental-health teams can standardize coordination

00:07:26.269 --> 00:07:28.359
notes with suitable information rules.

00:07:28.809 --> 00:07:32.309
Search-and-rescue teams can organize mission-preparation summaries.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.069
Security teams can structure patrol briefings, wildland

00:07:36.069 --> 00:07:40.090
coordinators can prepare seasonal orientation forms, and industrial

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:43.399
teams can retain system-training notes and a public handout.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.760
Across those settings, choose fields, numbering and client access for the task.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.780
Test the actual published form, verify the saved draft and

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.739
attachment, and retain the finalized revision that supports the entry.
